;;;; font.lisp --- a 5x7 bitmap font: every printable ASCII character, as ink.
;;;;
;;;; SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
;;;;
;;;; A frame is a monospaced grid of these glyphs, five columns by seven rows
;;;; each, '#' an inked pixel and '.' a blank one; rows are separated by a
;;;; slash so a table entry reads as the letter it draws. A character with no
;;;; entry of its own draws as the filled box, and so does every byte past
;;;; ASCII. The original plugin's renderer carried its own eval-tuned fonts;
;;;; this one is small enough to read and to check by eye.

(in-package #:nodecode-snapcompact)

